  "notes": "Purpose-built data-entry screen for non-technical volunteers transcribing paper meter sheets. Warm parchment background (#f3f0e8) with white panels and a deep teal header; accessibility-first type (Atkinson Hyperlegible + its mono with slashed zero for numbers). Each row shows previous reading, 12-month average, the always-editable new-reading input, computed use and a plain-language check ('Looks normal', 'Near zero, as expected'); flagged rows get a colored left edge and an outlined status button (red for 'Lower than previous', amber for 'Much higher than usual'). Clicking Review expands an in-row panel explaining 'What the numbers say' (previous vs typed vs difference), a correction field with 'one keystroke away' digit-typo suggestion chips, and an alternative path ('The meter was replaced or rolled over'). Sidebar tracks progress per route with reader names, a 'Next to enter' jump button, a review queue mirroring the flagged rows, and a 'Lock the cycle' gate whose dashed disabled button explains its preconditions. Keycap-styled shortcut legend at the bottom of the table. Local-first: 'Saved on this computer'."
